Every must-show item is on screen and nothing forbidden appears. The fold question is answered: the scrubber (x673–832, y31) and the position readout "128 / 1315" (x849–933, y31) are both in the identity bar, and the fill is 9.4% of the track against a true 128/1315 = 9.7%. This iteration's changes: (1) landed — the DATA note now sets flush-left in its own full-width row at a ~34-character measure; (2) unverifiable here — COST · TRANSACTIONFEE sits below y900, though the visible COST · MANA row reads "88000 / 200000" in base ten with no hex word; (3) unverifiable — no decoded-input note appears in this view; (4) landed — ⊘ on line 29, ⊙ on line 32; (5) landed — the exit reads "← demo", the badge "Synthetic demo data".

Typographically this is a dense, competent tool surface let down by one type treatment doing too many jobs. Pane titles (CODE, VALUES, TRANSACTION), the FRAME column header and the metadata row labels (DATA, BLOCK, TYPE) are all 9px-cap letterspaced caps separated only by a 162-vs-145 grey step, so three hierarchy levels look identical. The same total renders "1315" in the bar and "1,315" in the call trace. The DATA note is the pane's tallest block (193px, 23%) yet its quietest body text, and it is why the pane's tail is cut mid-line at y897.

Highest-priority fixes: split the caps scale into two levels; pick one thousands-separator rule.

Rating: 6/10

